WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.782
This example places two last-value calculations side by side.

00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:07.832
The first uses the default ordered frame.

00:00:07.832 --> 00:00:13.647
The second explicitly includes the entire partition, from the beginning through the end.

00:00:13.647 --> 00:00:16.587
Compare the two result columns carefully.

00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:23.212
The difference demonstrates why frame boundaries matter, especially for functions that ask for the first or last value

00:00:23.212 --> 00:00:24.649
in a sequence.
